  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "item": "theoreticalsciences:molten_salt_reactor",
      "title": "Molten Salt Reactor",
      "text": "Uranium dissolved in molten fluoride salt flows through a core of graphite and goes critical there. Tune it to exactly one neutron per neutron.$(br2)Generates power.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 2$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(thing)Made on the Extreme Assembly Table$() (it is also a crafting table). The recipe pages at the end of this entry - and JEI - show the pattern."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Burns $(item)Molten Salt Fuel$() for power and leaves $(item)Spent Fuel Salt$(). The fuel concentration and the control rods set k; the salt settles at the temperature where k is exactly 1 - keep it between 732 K (frozen) and 980 K (the vessel creeps). Its rejected heat goes into the coolant loop."
    },
